# No version or date here: a release is its git tag, which sets the package version
# through setuptools-scm, and Zenodo records both. Add the DOI under `identifiers`
# with the first Zenodo release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "rupture_generator: kinematic earthquake rupture generation"
abstract: >-
  Generates kinematic earthquake rupture models on multi-segment fault systems
  described in GeoJSON, and writes them as Standard Rupture Format files.
  A port and extension of genslip v5.6.2.
authors:
  - name: ucgmsim
  - family-names: Faulkner
    given-names: Jake
    affiliation: University of Canterbury
repository-code: "https://github.com/ucgmsim/rupture_generator"
url: "https://github.com/ucgmsim/rupture_generator"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - earthquake
  - kinematic rupture
  - ground motion simulation
  - standard rupture format
